  "name": "Human channelome \u2014 classify every catalogued pore-forming gene",
  "description": "The census target: every human gene the catalogue calls a pore-forming ion channel, classified from scratch through all three tiers with its gene symbol never consulted (hazard H15). `expected` is the catalogue's own assignment, so the run is simultaneously a census and a self-consistency test \u2014 a disagreement is either a classifier failure or a catalogue error, and both are worth finding. Roughly 320 genes at ~3 API calls each; budget 15-25 minutes.",
